[17592186344902 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344902 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344902 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344902 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344902 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344902 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186342400 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344902 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ebb4acd0-8375-525d-8189-262b00544043" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344946 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344946 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74608" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344946 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344946 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+4y-6z &=4 \\\\ 6x+12y-18z &=12 \\\\ -10x-20y+30z &=-20\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186344946 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "192e5819-2578-5d5d-bbaf-226710263b1b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344946 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 12 & -18 & 12 \\\\ -10 & -20 & 30 & -20\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 12 & -18 & 12 \\\\ -10 & -20 & 30 & -20\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 12 & -18 & 12 \\\\ -10 & -20 & 30 & -20\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & -20 & 30 & -20\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+10{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186344948 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344707 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344948 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74612" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344948 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344948 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-10y-5z &=10 \\\\ -10x+100y+50z &=-100 \\\\ -4x+40y+20z &=-40\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186344948 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f9c421da-e7e3-5854-9928-6f8234b711f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344948 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -10 & -5 & 10 \\\\ -10 & 100 & 50 & -100 \\\\ -4 & 40 & 20 & -40\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -10 & -5 & 10 \\\\ -10 & 100 & 50 & -100 \\\\ -4 & 40 & 20 & -40\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+10{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -10 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 40 & 20 & -40\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -10 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186344949 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344949 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74613" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344949 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344949 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x-6y+15z &=-3 \\\\ 6x+12y-30z &=6 \\\\ -6x-12y+30z &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186344949 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "78ef528f-61bb-5594-b0fa-7d95e275c2ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344949 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -6 & 15 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 12 & -30 & 6 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 30 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -6 & 15 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 12 & -30 & 6 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 30 & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 12 & -30 & 6 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 30 & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 30 & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-5z &=1 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations, we can remove these equations from the system. \n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables, $y,$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1-2y+5z \\\\ y &=y \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ and $z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1-2y+5z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186344951 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344951 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74617" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344951 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344951 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z &=3 \\\\ x+2y-2z &=0 \\\\ -2x+2y-2z &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186344951 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6b30e629-112f-508e-9e77-096b0e33781a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344951 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186344952 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344952 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74627" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344952 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344952 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-5y+5z &=-1 \\\\ -2x+10y &=-4 \\\\ x-5y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186344952 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "088ddf76-b8ab-5fdd-9fea-d3099bd8dbb5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344952 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & 5 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 10 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -5 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ into reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & 5 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 10 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -5 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 10 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5 & -5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+5z &=-3 \\\\ y+z &=-1 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation, we can remove this equation from the system. \n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-3-5z \\\\ y &=-z-1 \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3-5z \\\\ -z-1 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186390381 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186390382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390381 #edb/ref 1069 "q-20590" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390381 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390381 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=0 \\\\ y+2z &=0 \\\\ z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186390381 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9f45c2e0-9678-5cdd-b7f1-5fd5cc96fa80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390381 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form.\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186390382 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390382 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390382 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390382 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390386 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390382 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390382 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390382 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390382 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186390383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390382 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "13da932e-9b2a-5e64-abc3-8e5afbbc90ed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390383 #edb/ref 1080 "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186390383 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390383 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a91e48e3-62ec-5edb-bcf7-03d4a5806e0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390384 #edb/ref 1080 "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186390384 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390384 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5461c0a1-245b-5870-8efa-189453e52726" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390385 #edb/ref 1080 "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186390385 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390385 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0327ce18-3178-58df-99a3-60dc77f9fed2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390386 #edb/ref 1080 "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186390386 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390386 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fabd327a-4307-5856-a87b-ef1b6f25459d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390387 #edb/ref 1080 "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186390387 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390387 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "91ef62e9-3380-521c-8cbb-38d749ba6534" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400618 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400619 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400618 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131650" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400618 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400618 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-8y+12z &=-8 \\\\ x-2y+3z &=-2 \\\\ -2x+4y-6z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186400618 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b85625c7-6844-5453-a702-eb2fc4d7eb1b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400618 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8 & 12 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8 & 12 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 12 & -8 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+3z &=-2 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations, we can remove these equations from the system. \n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables, $y,$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2y-3z-2 \\\\ y &=y \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ and $z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2y-3z-2 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186400619 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400619 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400619 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400619 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400619 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400624 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400619 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400619 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400619 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186400621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400619 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "452119fd-5ef0-59d8-810c-92339d03e4d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400620 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}2-2y+3z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186400620 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400620 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bae6d20c-cc44-51fa-982c-3eec6a0de3e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400621 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}2y-3z-2 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186400621 #